Open with the thing itself, not with throat-clearing. The reader arrived for a
story, so tell it.

## Use headings to break the piece up

Body copy is set at a comfortable measure and is deliberately exempt from the
site-wide capitalisation rule — these are paragraphs, and title-casing prose
makes it unreadable.

Link to [a stop](/stops/bigfoot-trap) inline where it helps. The related-stops
list at the bottom is generated from the frontmatter, so it does not need
repeating in the text.

> Quotes render as pull quotes.

Keep sources honest. If something is contested, say it is contested — that is
more interesting than pretending otherwise, and it is the difference between
this and the rest of the internet on the subject.
